<article class="env-lemma" id="0E8K">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E8K">Lemma <span data-tag="0E8K">21.17.4</span>.</a> Let $(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{O})$ be a ringed site. Let $U$ be an object of $\mathcal{C}$. If $\mathcal{K}^\bullet $ is a K-flat complex of $\mathcal{O}$-modules, then $\mathcal{K}^\bullet |_ U$ is a K-flat complex of $\mathcal{O}_ U$-modules. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathcal{G}^\bullet $ be an exact complex of $\mathcal{O}_ U$-modules. Since $j_{U!}$ is exact (Modules on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/03DJ" data-tag="03DJ">18.19.3</a>) and $\mathcal{K}^\bullet $ is a K-flat complex of $\mathcal{O}$-modules we see that the complex 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  j_{U!}(\text{Tot}(\mathcal{G}^\bullet \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ U} \mathcal{K}^\bullet |_ U)) = \text{Tot}(j_{U!}\mathcal{G}^\bullet \otimes _\mathcal {O} \mathcal{K}^\bullet )  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is exact. Here the equality comes from Modules on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/0E8I" data-tag="0E8I">18.27.9</a> and the fact that $j_{U!}$ commutes with direct sums (as a left adjoint). We conclude because $j_{U!}$ reflects exactness by Modules on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/0E8G" data-tag="0E8G">18.19.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>